deep.reconstruction:
This folio contains no mathematics and no handwriting by Riemann. It is a printed page, numbered 13, of a 19th-century German antiquarian or second-hand bookseller's catalogue. The section heading is 'Naturwissenschaft und Physik', and the page runs alphabetically from Socin through Tscharner. It continues from page 12 (Schaeffer–Smith) and is followed by page 14 (Ule–Winckler).

Each entry gives:
- author and short title;
- format (8 = octavo, 4 = quarto, Fol. = folio, 12, Lex. 8);
- place and year, with the millennium dropped (e.g. '807' = 1807, '664' = 1664);
- binding (Ppbd. = Pappband, Hlbldrbd. = Halblederband, Pgmtbd. = Pergamentband, br. = brochirt, cart. = cartonnirt, Hlbpgmtbd., Hlblfzbd.);
- sometimes the original price in parentheses;
- the asking price in Thaler and Silbergroschen (1 Thaler = 30 Sgr).

The latest dated item is Süskind 1858. The previous page includes items dated 1860 and 1862. So the catalogue dates from about 1862 or later, close to or after Riemann's death in 1866. It was presumably filed with the papers incidentally, perhaps as scrap paper or as a wrapper.

There are no derivations to reconstruct. The only arithmetic on the page is price notation, such as fractions of a Thaler and Sgr amounts like 7½ Sgr. The page is relevant only as a curiosity: it hints at an interest in, or exposure to, the second-hand trade in natural-science books.
